"""Hedging modals and habit/likelihood adverbs.

Layer-0 MLP output component 5305 reads words that come just before a verb or predicate
and say how strongly, how often or how likely something is. It goes strongly negative on:
- Chinese obligation and advice modals: 必须 (must), 应 / 應 (should), 须, 宜, 最好
  (had better), 只能 (can only), 不得 (must not), 不应;
- 会 / 會 used as a modal ("will", "tends to"), and 肯定 / 一般 / 通常 / 常常;
- English adverbs of habit or likelihood: usually, typically, preferably, normally.
Milder negatives: 需要, 需 (need), 要 (want to), 可以, 能 (can), 可能 (possibly), probably,
likely, commonly, rarely, generally, often.
Small positives: the word "assistant" right after <|im_start|> (the start of a model
turn), and a few auxiliaries/words: could, would, ever, already, 有, 该, </tool_response>.
English modal auxiliaries (can, will, should, must) and most other tokens stay near zero.
The program predicts from the current token and the one before it; it has no state.
"""

READS = ()

STRONG = {
    "必须": -1.3, "必須": -1.3, "应": -1.3, "應": -1.3, "须": -1.3, "須": -1.3,
    "宜": -1.3, "最好": -1.3, "只能": -1.2, "不得": -1.2, "不应": -1.2,
    "会": -0.8, "會": -0.8, "不会": -0.8, "不能": -0.8, "都会": -0.9, "可能会": -0.9,
    "肯定会": -1.0, "应该": -0.8, "一般": -0.7, "通常": -1.0, "肯定": -0.8, "常常": -0.8,
    "usually": -0.95, "typically": -0.85, "preferably": -1.0, "normally": -0.5,
}
MILD = {
    "需要": -0.5, "需": -0.6, "要": -0.35, "可以": -0.4, "能": -0.35, "可能": -0.5,
    "必": -0.6, "只好": -0.5, "才能": -0.5, "可": -0.25,
    "probably": -0.45, "likely": -0.35, "commonly": -0.25, "rarely": -0.3,
    "generally": -0.2, "often": -0.17,
}
POSITIVE = {
    "could": 0.1, "would": 0.06, "ever": 0.1, "already": 0.07, "有": 0.14, "该": 0.3,
    "</tool_response>": 0.12,
}
ASSISTANT_AFTER_TURN_START = 0.27


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    tok = prefix.token_strings[-1].strip()
    prev = prefix.token_strings[-2] if len(prefix) > 1 else ""
    if tok in STRONG:
